# Do these names tell the truth?
subtitle: "Three famous names, three fibs: guess how long the Hundred Years' War lasted, where Panama hats are made and where guinea pigs come from."
tags: ["misleading names","etymology","south america"]
teaches: ["history/conflict-duration","geography/product-origins","vocabulary/naming-origins","concepts/misnomers"]
voices: {"a":"gemini:Charon | a warm, clear quiz host who loves a good fact; patient, natural pace","b":"gemini:Pulcherrima | a forward co-host who says what most people think; natural, never exaggerated","take":"lines"}
format: quiz

## Do these names tell the truth?
feedback:
    style: warm
    perfect: Nobody's name fools you.
    good: You saw through most of them.
    poor: These names have fooled people for centuries.
    none: The names won this round.
affirm: playful
sources:
    - id: hyw
      title: Hundred Years' War
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2025
      finding: intermittent conflict between England and France, 1337-1453
    - id: hat
      title: Traditional weaving of the Ecuadorian toquilla straw hat
      authors: UNESCO
      year: 2012
      finding: the so-called Panama hat is woven in Ecuador from toquilla palm fibre; inscribed on the Intangible Cultural Heritage list in 2012
    - id: cavy
      title: Guinea pig
      authors: Encyclopaedia Britannica
      year: 2025
      finding: a South American rodent, domesticated in the Andes thousands of years ago; still raised for food there
    - id: cuy
      title: National Guinea Pig Day (Día Nacional del Cuy)
      authors: Peru, Ministry of Agriculture (reported by TreXperience Peru)
      year: 2013
      url: https://trexperienceperu.com/travel-news/national-guinea-pig-day-adorable-symbol-culture-and-nutrition-peru
      finding: since 2013 Peru marks National Cuy Day on the second Friday of October, with fairs and festivals promoting breeding and eating guinea pigs

    sequence names items [{"icon":{"of":"crossed swords","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Hundred Years' War","mark":{"text":"116 years","color":"#b5482e"}},{"icon":{"of":"womans hat","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Panama hat","mark":{"text":"Ecuador","color":"#b5482e"}},{"icon":{"of":"mouse face","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Guinea pig","mark":{"text":"Andes","color":"#b5482e"}}] show_upcoming dots hidden true

    card title "Do these names tell the truth?"

A: Three famous names, and every one of them tells a fib. Can you spot where?
    draw names_dot_1 names_dot_2 names_dot_3 parallel true

A: First, the Hundred Years' War, between England and France.
    draw names_1

    quiz "How long did the Hundred Years' War last?" id war on_canvas true say_question true reveal "116 years" buttons_at.x 810 buttons_at.y 430 buttons_layout column
        right: A hundred and sixteen years: England and France fought on and off from 1337 to 1453.
        * 99 years
        * 100 years
        + 116 years

B: A hundred and sixteen? I'd have said a hundred, obviously.
    highlight war_stamp

B: Next one. The Panama hat. Surely that one's safe?
    draw names_2

    quiz "So where are Panama hats really made?" id hat on_canvas true say_question true reveal Ecuador buttons_at.x 810 buttons_at.y 430 buttons_layout column
        right: Ecuador. They are woven from toquilla palm straw, around towns like Montecristi and Cuenca.
        * Panama
        + Ecuador
        * Cuba

A: They were shipped out through Panama, and the workers who dug the canal wore them.
    highlight names_2_label

B: And the guinea pig. At least that's from Guinea?
    draw names_3

    quiz "Where do guinea pigs come from?" id pig on_canvas true say_question true reveal "The Andes" buttons_at.x 810 buttons_at.y 430 buttons_layout column
        right: The Andes of South America, where people tamed them thousands of years ago, and still eat them today.
        * Guinea
        + The Andes
        * New Guinea

B: So not from Guinea at all. Peru even gives it a national day every October, with fairs and feasts.
    text cuyday "Peru: Cuy Day" #2f6b8f cites ["cuy"] x 800 y 340 font_size 46

    hide cuyday

A: Let us line them up. Three names, three fibs.
    draw names_strip

A: As for the guinea pig: it's a rodent. It just squeals a bit like a piglet.
    highlight names_3
---
